course: dictionary
lesson: 4631
title: Hilly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hilly means having a lot of hills. A hilly place has lots of slopes that go up and down. When you read «hilly countryside», picture a land full of hills, not one single hill.
explain: Read the words around hilly to get more clues. In «Ponies are often from cold hilly places like Shetland, Wales or Dartmoor», the places named are where the land has many hills, and the ponies are used to it.
explain: Hilly places change how people live and move. In «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes», the farmers build flat steps on the slopes so the soil does not wash away. In a hilly route, you climb up and down many times, so the run or ride takes longer.
fact: Hilly means having a lot of hills.
fact: «Hilly countryside» means land with many hills in it.
fact: The Pennines, the Lake District and Wales are hilly areas in Britain.
fact: Farmers in hilly places cut flat steps called terraces into the slopes, so soil stays in place and water is held.
fact: Ponies from hilly places like Dartmoor and Shetland have thick coats for wind and rain.
exercise: «Farmers in hilly places cut steps called terraces into the slopes.» What does hilly mean here? | Covered in water | *Having a lot of hills | Very hot and dry | Flat and wide with no slopes
exercise: Which of these is a hilly area? | A flat beach with no slopes | A flat desert | An empty car park | *The Lake District
exercise: «Ponies are often from cold hilly places like Shetland, Wales or Dartmoor.» Which place is named as a hilly place? | *Dartmoor | Madrid | Paris | London
test: The Rat says the dell «seems all hilly and humpy and hummocky». What does hilly mean here? | Smooth and flat | Hot and dry | Full of water | *Having lots of hills and bumps
test: Why does a hilly route take longer to run or cycle? | Because the route is shorter | Because the route is only on a flat road | Because it is always raining | *Because you must climb and go down many slopes
exam: In a story, «a hilly road might make a journey» feel like what? | *Tiring | Shorter | Free | Silent
